      "title": "How Kraft Heinz Is Reshaping Its Portfolio for Long-Term Growth",
      "summary": "Kraft Heinz has agreed to sell its North America coffee business, including brands like Maxwell House and Gevalia, to One Rock Capital Partners for $650 million while retaining a 30% equity stake. The company expects approximately $500 million in after-tax proceeds to be used for debt repayment. The transaction is expected to close in mid-2027 and is anticipated to be growth and margin accretive while strengthening Kraft Heinz's financial flexibility.",
